 {
  "path": "schemas/note-format.md",
  "text": "# Note format\n\nEvery note (except this folder and `README.md`) starts with a header between two `---` lines. The build\n(`scripts/brain/build.mjs`) refuses a note whose header is missing a required field or uses an unknown value.\n\n```markdown\n---\nid: lrv-bookings\ntitle: Booking La Rosa View\nbrand: la-rosa-view\ntype: topic\nvisibility: public\nstatus: verified\naliases: [book La Rosa, hire the DJ, booking request, réserver, حجز]\ntags: [booking, event, hire]\nsources: [site-booking-form, site-terms]\nupdated: 2026-10-29\n---\n```\n\n| Field | Required | Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `id` | yes | Unique, lower case, letters, digits and dashes. Never reuse an id. |\n| `title` | yes | The note's name; `[[links]]` use it (or an alias). |\n| `brand` | yes | `houcine-world` (shared), `la-rosa-view`, `houcine-tech`, `houcine-studio`, `houcine-management`, `houcine-education`. A new brand is added in `supabase/functions/_shared/brain/compile.ts` (`BRANDS`). |\n| `type` | yes | `overview`, `topic`, `service`, `person`, `policy`, `faq`, `contact`, `relationship`, `index`, `source`, `agent` (`index`, `source` and `agent` notes are never searched). |\n| `visibility` | yes | `public` (an agent may use it), `internal` (owner and maintainers only), `confidential` (never leaves the repository). Only `public` is compiled into the agents' index. |\n| `status` | yes | The note's default reliability: `verified`, `policy` (a current rule), `incomplete`, `pending` (awaiting confirmation), `outdated` (kept for history, never stated as current). |\n| `sources` | yes for public notes | Ids from `sources/` (the build checks that each exists). |\n| `updated` | yes | The date the facts were last checked, `YYYY-MM-DD`. |\n| `aliases` | no | Other names for the subject, in any language. Links and search use them. |\n| `tags` | no | Short keywords that help search. |\n| `fact_<name>` | no | One machine-readable value that code also needs (for example `fact_email`). A test compares it with the site's own constant. |\n\n## Status inside a note\n\nA section can say it is less certain than the note as a whole: put a callout as the first line under its heading.\n\n```markdown\n## Prices\n> [!incomplete] No price or package is published for La Rosa View.\n```\n\nCallouts understood: `[!verified]`, `[!policy]`, `[!incomplete]`, `[!pending]`, `[!outdated]`. The agent is told\nthe status of every passage it receives, and never states an `incomplete`, `pending` or `outdated` passage as a\ncurrent fact.\n\n## Links\n\n`[[Title]]` or `[[Title|shown text]]` links to another note by its title or one of its aliases. The build fails on a\nlink that matches no note. Links are also how search finds related notes: when a note is a good match, the best part\nof each note it links to is considered too (only within the brands the agent may use).\n\n## Sections become passages\n\nThe search works on passages: each `##` section of a note is one passage (with the note's title and header). Keep\na section about one thing, and give it a heading that says what it is about.\n\n## AI access notes (`agents/`)\n\nA note with `type: agent` says which brands one AI agent may read. Extra header fields: `agent` (the agent's id),\n`brands` (full access to their public notes), `referral_brands` (only their public overview), `fallback_note` and\n`pinned` (passage ids always sent). Edited in Knowledge Studio, Settings, AI access. Only public notes are ever\ncompiled, so no access setting can expose an internal or restricted note.\n\n## Archived notes (`archive/`)\n\nA note moved into `archive/` keeps its file and history but is never compiled; an active note may not link to it\n(the build names the link to remove first). Knowledge Studio archives and restores notes by moving them.\n"
 },
 {
  "path": "sources/website.md",
  "text": "---\nid: sources-website\ntitle: Sources on the public site\nbrand: houcine-world\ntype: source\nvisibility: public\nstatus: verified\nupdated: 2026-10-29\n---\n\n# Sources on the public site\n\nEach id below is a place the facts in the brain were read from. A note lists the ids it relies on in `sources`.\nWhen one of these pages changes, the notes that cite it must be checked again.\n\n<!-- source ids: one per line, \"- `id`: where\" -->\n- `site-larosaview`: the La Rosa View page, `/larosaview` (`src/pages/LaRosaView.tsx`)\n- `site-about-dj`: the DJ page, `/about-dj` (`src/pages/AboutDJ.tsx`)\n- `site-booking-form`: the booking request form, `/booking` (`src/pages/BookingForm.tsx`)\n- `site-review`: the review form, `/review` (`src/pages/Review.tsx`)\n- `site-terms`: the Terms, `/terms` (`src/pages/Terms.tsx`)\n- `site-contact`: the contact page, `/contact` (`src/pages/Contact.tsx`) and `src/config/contact.ts`\n- `site-legal-data`: the ecosystem and managed-brand lists of the legal pages (`src/data/legal.ts`)\n- `site-services`: the four verticals (`src/content/services.ts`)\n- `site-faq`: the ecosystem questions (`src/content/faq.ts`)\n- `site-dev`: the Houcine.tech page, `/dev`, and its catalogue (`src/content/techCatalogue.ts`)\n- `site-designs`: the Houcine.studio page, `/designs`, and its packages (`src/data/servicePackages.ts`)\n- `site-reads`: the Houcine.education page, `/reads`\n- `site-manages`: the Houcine.management page, `/manages`\n- `owner-confirmation-2026-10-30`: the owner, in the Knowledge Studio epic (GitHub issue #74): Houcine.education is both a curated digital bookstore and an educational service in development, not yet open\n- `previous-concierge`: the facts the concierge used before the brain (`supabase/functions/concierge/knowledgeBase.ts`, retired 29 October 2026), all of them taken from the pages above\n"
 }
